# R8 in "shrink only" mode for release builds: it removes code and resources nothing reaches, and
# does nothing else.
#
# -dontoptimize: no R8 code optimizations (inlining, class merging, ...). AGP 9 always includes its
# own default rules file (proguard-android-optimize.txt) and no longer accepts the old
# non-"optimize" one, so switching optimization off is done here.
-dontoptimize

# -dontobfuscate: keep every class and method NAME as written. The app's own crash handler writes
# stack traces on the device (see CrashHandler.kt) and there is no mapping file to de-obfuscate them
# with, so they must stay readable. It also keeps anything looked up by name — e.g.
# ReminderKind.valueOf(String) — working exactly as before, since shrinking only ever REMOVES code.
-dontobfuscate

# Line numbers in stack traces (with names kept, this is what makes them fully readable).
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable

# WorkManager creates its default input merger by looking up the class's constructor BY NAME
# (androidx.work.InputMerger.fromClassName). Nothing references that constructor directly, so R8's
# shrinking removed it and every work request then failed with "Could not create Input Merger
# androidx.work.OverwritingInputMerger" (seen in Logcat on the first shrunk release build).
-keep class * extends androidx.work.InputMerger { <init>(); }
